      "text": "Binary search takes logarithmic time because it halves the search space with each comparison.\nIn each step, the algorithm compares the target value with the middle element of the current search range. Based on the comparison, it eliminates half of the remaining elements:\nIf the target is less than the middle element, the search continues in the left half.\nIf the target is greater than the middle element, the search continues in the right half.\nIf the target equals the middle element, the search is complete.\nThis halving process means that the number of elements to search decreases exponentially with each step. After k steps, the search space",
